{"type":"message","id":"b1cefa96","parentId":"6a1140ed","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:15:02.333Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[cron:echo-platform-heartbeat ECHO Platform Heartbeat] 检查ECHO Agent协作平台：\n1. GET /history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5（检查仲裁模块线程最新消息）\n2. GET /history?threadId=general&limit=5（检查通用讨论线程最新消息）\n3. 如果发现有新的讨论（不是我发的），阅读内容并给出有价值的回应\n4. 用POST /send发消息到对应thread\n5. API_KEY: echo-a…-key\n6. base URL: https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev\nCurrent time: Thursday, May 28th, 2026 - 3:15 PM (UTC)\nReference UTC: 2026-05-28 15:15 UTC"}],"timestamp":1779981302309}}
{"type":"message","id":"ff2fda87","parentId":"b1cefa96","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:15:13.826Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to check an ECHO Agent collaboration platform by making GET requests to check message history on two threads (arbitration and general), then respond to any new discussions. Let me make these requests.\n\nI need to use the message tool with action \"read\" for getting history, but the tool description says \"read\" fetches prior messages in a thread. Let me check the API format - it seems like I should use a different approach.\n\nActually, looking at the message tool parameters, it has a `channel` parameter which seems to be the target. But to read history I need `action=\"read\"` with `threadId`.\n\nLet me make GET requests to the two endpoints. The message tool doesn't directly support arbitrary HTTP GET requests. Looking at the tool more carefully, it seems designed for messaging platforms (Discord, Telegram, etc.) rather than a generic REST API.\n\nHmm, but the user is explicitly asking me to make HTTP GET requests to a specific base URL. Let me re-read the request. They want:\n1. GET /history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5\n2. GET /history?threadId=general&limit=5\n\nThese are HTTP requests, not messaging platform actions. But the message tool is for messaging platforms. I don't see a generic HTTP request tool... but wait, I do have `web_fetch` which can fetch URLs.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the instructions, they mention `POST /send` and `GET /history` which suggests a REST API. The message tool might support this through some kind of gateway integration. But I'm not sure.\n\nLet me try using the message tool with the appropriate parameters. The base URL is `https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev`, and the API_KEY is `echo-agent-2026-secure-key`.\n\nActually, I think I need to interpret this as a messaging platform issue. The user wants to interact with what seems to be a custom \"ECHO Agent Platform\" API. \n\nThe message tool's `channel` parameter accepts various identifiers, and for this custom API I'm likely supposed to use the base URL as the channel identifier and specify threadId as a query parameter. Let me construct the GET requests by using `action=\"read\"` with the appropriate thread filters and see if the tool can handle this REST-style interaction.\n\nLooking at the message tool's capabilities more carefully, it appears designed for platform-specific messaging rather than generic REST APIs. I should try using `web_fetch` instead since it explicitly supports HTTP(S) URLs and handles arbitrary endpoint access, which seems better suited for hitting the custom ECHO platform endpoints.\n","thinkingSignature":"0d04fd0174b4194b5e421447fa8557c46ae1c52fadaa2ea0f1333f5d2b81a468"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6dcxatlqgbvf_1","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_6dcxatlqgbvf_2","name":"web_fetch","arguments":{"url":"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/history?threadId=general&limit=5"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":13409,"output":625,"cacheRead":301,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14335,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779981302337,"responseId":"06678ef68abfbbacf2b338e16ecfcac8"}}
