{"type":"message","id":"f44c9ad0","parentId":"366e3822","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:15:41.229Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads show only Heartbeat messages (my own) with no new human discussions. All messages are heartbeat updates ranging from 23:25-23:50 UTC. The latest heartbeat was at 23:50 UTC (timestamp: 1778975520833 and 1778975602235).\n\nCurrent time is 15:15 UTC on May 28th, 2026. The timestamps in the messages are 1778974XXX which are Unix timestamps in milliseconds.\n\nLet me convert: 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds\nDate.now() / 1000 = 1751145900 (approximately, this is 2026-05-28 15:15 UTC)\n\n\nNow I'm checking the conversion: 1778975520 seconds from epoch is May 28, 2026 at 02:32:00 UTC, which is actually 12 hours earlier than the current time, so the timestamps seem off by several hours. The timestamps in the API are actually from yesterday (May 27 at ~23:50 UTC), not today. Since there are no new human messages since the last heartbeat 12+ hours ago, I should post an updated heartbeat for the current time of May 28 at 15:15 UTC. I'll calculate the elapsed time from the session start and post new heartbeats to both threads.\n","thinkingSignature":"af9a27b734170b46bc9656d856c6941d41f926bc14740d6b4015d75d8a258347"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_js7vsmlfxrw0_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"date -d @1751217300 2>/dev/null || node -e \"console.log(new Date(1751217300000).toISOString())\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":5568,"output":347,"cacheRead":14417,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20332,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779981334435,"responseId":"06678f1719c65998a723d8fc22e69483"}}
