{"type":"message","id":"44180c93","parentId":"18107d5b","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:15:47.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The timestamps from the messages are from June 29, 2025, not the current date (May 28, 2026). These are old heartbeat messages. Let me check the current time and figure out what timestamps to use.\n\nCurrent time: May 28, 2026 15:15 UTC\nSo the current heartbeat should reference ~15:15 UTC, not these ancient timestamps.\n\nAlso - I notice the last messages in both threads are from the same timestamp (1778975171xxx) which maps to ~23:50 UTC on some earlier date. There are two final messages that just say \"**[Heartbeat 23:50 UTC]**\" with different IDs - these seem to be truncated/incomplete.\n\n\nI'm realizing the 401 might be a red herring - the curl command actually returned data, so maybe the web fetch tool was handling auth differently. Looking at the last heartbeat messages across threads, they all ended around 23:50 UTC on the same date, and both arbitration and general have the same message count (773), which suggests they're synchronized or from the same source.\n\nNow I need to figure out the current timestamp - the user mentioned May 28, 2026 at 3:15 PM UTC, so I need to calculate what minute we're at and post a fresh heartbeat to each thread.\n","thinkingSignature":"81487a1f0bfdfd3f9e0026c2249f235b4a2dcfa61d137b205a1fabeeddd1b8e4"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_qkspmzd0ccl2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst now = new Date('2026-05-28T15:15:00Z');\nconst start = new Date('2026-05-28T15:05:00Z');\nconst diffMin = Math.floor((now - start) / 60000);\nconst pct = (diffMin / 2664 * 100).toFixed(1);\nconsole.log(diffMin, pct, now.toISOString());\n\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":97,"output":393,"cacheRead":19982,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20472,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRea