{"type":"message","id":"3323f553","parentId":"1f63c9f8","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:16:01.311Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the picture. The last heartbeat messages in both threads were from ~23:50 UTC (based on the older cron schedule). The timestamps 1778975520833 and 1778975602235 correspond to approximately June 29, 2025 - but the cron is triggering now at 2026-05-28 15:15 UTC (10 minutes after the \"start\" of 15:05).\n\nThe cron expects me to generate a heartbeat as if it were much later (around minute 750+). The system appears to be running on an old schedule where heartbeats were sent every 5 minutes from 15:05 UTC. The last heartbeats were around 23:50 UTC on that schedule (minute 750+), but we're currently at 15:15 UTC (minute 10).\n\n","thinkingSignature":"c343e52adc09d97e309de9b6159b3fd67fe8ed483bcbcb759f78bf9d6bda20ef"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_3swowxtz928a_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst start = new Date('2026-05-28T15:05:00Z');\nconst now = new Date('2026-05-28T15:15:00Z');\nconst diffMin = Math.floor((now - start) / 60000);\nconst pct = (diffMin / 2664 * 100).toFixed(1);\nconsole.log('minutes:', diffMin, 'pct:', pct + '%');\n\"","timeout":10}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":1652,"output":297,"cacheRead":20235,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22184,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779981355968,"responseId":"06678f2c610543909b493b4d96a889f5"}}
