{"type":"message","id":"52edb5e8","parentId":"238f53e9","timestamp":"2026-05-28T15:18:27.517Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Cloudflare edge is returning a 500 with \"error code: 1101\". This looks like a Cloudflare error code (Error 1101 = \"Worker thrown exception\" or something similar - actually 1101 is \"Worker not deployed\"? Let me check. Actually CF 1101 is \"Worker threw an error\". So the worker at that route is throwing an exception.\n\nThe /health endpoint returns 200. The /history endpoint works with auth. But /send throws a Cloudflare Worker error 1101.\n\nThis is an internal server error in the Cloudflare Worker - something in the send handler is crashing. The authentication is working (we're getting past auth and hitting the worker code), but the worker itself is throwing an error.\n\n\nI should probably report this to the user, but I'm also wondering if there's a rate limiting issue or if the message queue is backed up, though that wouldn't typically throw a 1101. Let me try a simpler test to see if the endpoint just doesn't work at all.\n","thinkingSignature":"9b96be6839ad87ef086a8384ded757c3a19d4060cc1a06d73f86e01cb3d936da"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_t58pn7vgphma_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Test various approaches\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\"}' 2>&1\n\necho \"---\"\n\n# Try without messageId field at all\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test\",\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1}}' 2>&1","timeout":15}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-po